Local change to the vendored TinyUSB dwc2 host driver: the hcd_dwc2.c half of
our upstream PR "dwc2 host: CFG_TUH_DWC2_POLLED keeps the controller interrupt
off" (dp111/tinyusb branch dwc2-host-polled, 54c1b6133).  The PR's other half
gives CFG_TUH_DWC2_POLLED a default of 0 in tusb_option.h; tusb_config.h
defines it here, so this file is all the build needs.  Delete this file and
its CMake step (src/CMakeLists.txt, HCD_DWC2_PATCHED) once the submodule pin
contains the PR.  The build applies it to a copy of hcd_dwc2.c in the build
tree and compiles that; the submodule itself stays a plain upstream pin.

hcd_init enables the controller's global interrupt output a moment after it
powers the port; on a Raspberry Pi the first host-mode interrupt then resets
the board.  With CFG_TUH_DWC2_POLLED the output is never enabled and usb.c
polls tuh_int_handler instead, so there is no window at all.

diff --git a/src/portable/synopsys/dwc2/hcd_dwc2.c b/src/portable/synopsys/dwc2/hcd_dwc2.c
index 19698b215..2b7653acf 100644
--- a/src/portable/synopsys/dwc2/hcd_dwc2.c
+++ b/src/portable/synopsys/dwc2/hcd_dwc2.c
@@ -718,7 +718,9 @@ bool hcd_init(uint8_t rhport, const tusb_rhport_init_t* rh_init) {
 
   // NPTX can hold at least 2 packet, change interrupt level to half-empty
   uint32_t gahbcfg = dwc2->gahbcfg & ~GAHBCFG_TX_FIFO_EPMTY_LVL;
-  gahbcfg |= GAHBCFG_GINT;   // Enable global interrupt
+  if (!CFG_TUH_DWC2_POLLED) {
+    gahbcfg |= GAHBCFG_GINT; // Enable global interrupt, unless the application polls tuh_int_handler()
+  }
   dwc2->gahbcfg = gahbcfg;
 
   return true;
